Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:58:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] guest: mount retained encrypted volumes through CDH

Reuse the CDH SecureMount API for retained devices with embedded LUKS
headers. Bind disk identities and key references to measured workspace
policy, and invoke the measured cryptsetup initializer only when that
policy permits initialization.

Check the active LUKS2 mapping for AES-XTS with a 512-bit key and
4096-byte sectors before exposing a measured workspace. Preserve
readonly behavior and roll back only mounts and mappings acquired by the
current call.

Apply fsGroup recursively to retained content without changing owners or
following paths outside the volume. Preserve readonly mounts and set the
directory setgid bit so newly created files inherit the requested group.

